      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T23:17:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can\u0027t use global data, it breaks testing.  You can attach data to the context using something like https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/sdk_library.go;l\u003d2280-2286;drc\u003d00e0991f702751098fe95c0dfce5cd3725659abf, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s necessary here.  \n\nThe reinitialization is an artifact of needing to be able to clone modules to create variants, combined with limitations of Go\u0027s reflection functionality.  We can\u0027t clone arbitrary types or unexported values, so the only data that gets cloned is the property structs.\n\nIf you need to store data from mutators for use later, use a [Provider](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/blueprint/provider.go;l\u003d85;drc\u003d7add62142d6d75bdef9eb788ecb59bae9bb04421).",
